ht|n|at|^*GA1,1.  A 6-4 is still considered a one suited hand^*N|
                  
ht|o|at|^*GA2,2.  Ogust^*N|
                  
ht|p|at|^*GA3,3.  With 4-4 in minors Howard opens 1@C unless the diamonds are stronger^*N|
                  
ht|q|at|^*GA4,4.  When you have 2 cue bids available^*N|
                  
ht|r|at|^*GA5,5.  Law of Total Tricks is a very good guideline on competitive auctions^*N|
                  
ht|s|at|^*GA6,6.  Is 4-4 fit better than 5-3 fit ? ^*N|


