qx|A1|st||rh||ah|Board 1 IMPs   -   August 21, 2024|pn|hondo717,aspiring,vs_bbo,rustgi65|
md|3SK6542HJTD952CA94,SJ73HK73DJTCJT732,ST8HAQ62DQ87643C8,SAQ9H9854DAKCKQ65|sv|0|
mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would have opened 2@D with the North hand. Some play that they won't open a Weak-2 with an outside 4-card major. I consider that is incorrect. Also some feel they need a reasonably strong suit, although having a 6-card suit gives you some strength in and of itself.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


mb|1N|mb|PP?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now North should make a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dont,DONT^*N|CP||FP||at| double to show a one suited hand. A 6-4 is still considered a one suited hand. There are very few hands where it ends up being better to play in a 4-card suit than 6-card suit.|SB|SAlso, I see now that East was too strong for 1N. Didn't notice before. We let it stand.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
