https://tinyurl.com/2dmb255a
qx|A2|st||rh||ah|Board 2 IMPs   -   August 21, 2024|pn|hondo717,aspiring,vs_bbo,rustgi65|
md|4SKT7HAQDJ73CK6543,SA9HT873DAQ64CAQ2,S64HK654DK985CJT7,SQJ8532HJ92DT2C98|sv|n|
mb|2S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|At this vulnerability 2@S is possible, although East is a little light for the bid. However, at favorable vulnerability (you are not vulnerable, they are) you should stretch your preempts, particularly in 1st seat and 3rd seat. |
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would have preferred better distribution. Hands with singletons and voids are much better for preempting. But 2@S is certainly possible and as you can see gives me a problem.|
PG| ***** 27 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2N|an|please describe your hand|
PG| ***** 28 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Over Weak-2 bids many play ^*BFeature^*n where over 2N, partner bids a suit where they have an outside ace or king or bid 3@S with the hand they have. |
PG| ***** 29 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|However, I prefer |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ogust,Ogust^*N|CP||FP||at|. All responses by Weak-2 bidder to 2N are artificial and describe two parts of his hand.
^cHow "good" the suit is -- a good suit contains two of the top 3 honors, and
^cHow strong the hand is -- a strong hand is 8-10 points.|
PG| ***** 30 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The responses to 2N |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ogust,Ogust^*N|CP||FP||at| are:
^C3@C = weak hand bad suit;
^C3@D = weak hand good suit;
^c3@H = strong hand bad suit, and
^c3@S = strong hand strong suit.|
PG| ***** 31 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So East's response is 3@C = bad hand and bad suit. |
PG| ***** 32 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Please note that playing |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ogust,Ogust^*N|CP||FP||at|, if I were West and East had shown a good suit meaning their suit had the @SK and @SQ I would have bid 3N, because West can count 6 spade tricks (assuming a 3-2 break) and 2 aces for sure and is likely to be able to take one more trick.|
PG| ***** 33 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And over 3@H (good hand bad suit) I would have bid 4@S. However, I agree with 3@S by West given the 3@C bid.|
PG| ***** 34 ***** |


mb|P|mb|3S|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 35 ***** |


