%%%%%%Hand 3
https://tinyurl.com/2cu5aegd
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   August 21, 2024|pn|hondo717,hondo717,aspiring,rustgi65|
md|1SKQT2HK86DT42CQT3,SAJ973HJ953DJCJ52,S65HAQTD98753CA97,S84H742DAKQ6CK864|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|P|mb|P?|mb|1D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Most players, with 4-4 in the minors, open 1@D. That is okay. However, I more often than not open 1@C as that keeps the auction lower and more flexible. But with East's hand, with diamonds so much better than clubs, even I would open 1@D.|
PG| ***** 51 ***** |


mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I don't love my hand, but with no wasted cards in diamonds and the fact that I passed already, meaning my hand can't be all that good I will make a light takeout double. If in my place you chose to pass, that would be fine also.|
PG| ***** 52 ***** |


mb|D|mb|1S|mb|P|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally 1@S is forcing but because West is a passed hand, it is no longer forcing. But I still think East should bid 1N instead of passing. West may very well have only 4 spades.|
PG| ***** 53 ***** |


 

mb|P|
pg| ***** 54 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|S6|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North has no good lead. I probably would not lead a spade for the following reason. I doubled meaning I have something in spades and a spade lead is finessing me. On the other hand, a diamond is not a great lead either because East opened 1@D. |
PG| ***** 55 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And leading an unprotected ace is not great either. I probably choose either a diamond (which does not work particularly well here) or the @HA, because of my double it is somewhat more likely I have the @HK.|
PG| ***** 56 ***** |


